# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Crochet & Co. — environment
#
# There is exactly one variable left, and it is optional.
#
# Everything this file used to describe is gone:
#
#   DATABASE_URL               Supabase Postgres  →  data/catalog.sqlite
#   SUPABASE_URL               Supabase Storage    →  apps/web/public/images/
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY  a master password   →  nothing; there are no secrets
#   BETTER_AUTH_SECRET         session signing     →  nothing; the panel is loopback-only
#   BETTER_AUTH_URL            auth origin         →  nothing
#   BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS CORS allowlist     →  nothing; no cross-origin requests
#   PUBLIC_API_URL             the API             →  nothing; the build reads catalog.json
#   PUBLIC_AUTH_URL            the auth origin     →  nothing
#   PORT                       the listener        →  4322, hardcoded in vite.config.ts
#   PAGES_DEPLOY_HOOK          the rebuild trigger →  `git push` to main
#
# None of them are replaced by a new secret. The panel has no credentials
# because it binds to 127.0.0.1 and there is no network path to it; the build
# has no credentials because it reads one committed JSON file; and publishing
# uses the git push you already have.
#
# So there is nothing here to leak, and nothing to rotate.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Storefront (apps/web) — the only build-time variable.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Public origin of the storefront. Used for canonical URLs, the sitemap and
# social cards. Must be the real deployed origin, or every canonical tag and
# sitemap entry points somewhere that is not the site.
PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://crochet-and-co.pages.dev"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Admin panel (apps/admin) — optional, and rarely needed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the SQLite catalogue lives. Defaults to data/catalog.sqlite at the
# workspace root.
#
# The only reason to set this is to keep two catalogues side by side — a real
# shop and a scratch one for trying a promotion out, say. It is gitignored
# wherever it points.
#
#   CROCHET_DB=/home/you/shop-prod.sqlite
# CROCHET_DB=
